# Used only by `npm run build:tauri` (vite build --mode tauri), which feeds
# the desktop app's installer. Unlike the web build, there's no dev-server
# proxy to ride through - the app talks straight to this absolute origin, so
# it must be reachable from wherever the installed app will run (an office
# LAN IP, or a stable ngrok domain for off-site use).
#
# Copy this file to .env.tauri and fill in a real, reachable origin before
# running `npm run tauri:build`. This value is baked into the installer at
# build time - see TAURI_SETUP.md for what that means for switching servers
# later.
VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.0.178:4000/api
